=== chapter3_intro

{poet_name}'s eyes softened at the pain in her voice, but it also seemed to harden something in him. 

# speaker: {poet_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/poet_sprite
"The burden is not yours to shoulder, at least not alone." 

He said, his tone turning sharp as he focuses on {king_name}. 

# speaker: {poet_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/poet_sprite
"Maybe the army would have been better prepared if they knew what was coming. Maybe they could have anticipated this attack if the first one had not been covered up."

 {king_name}'s eyes blazed, the same way they used to when {poet_name} managed to get under her skin when they were kids.
 
# speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
 "You speak so freely now. Yet when the crown begged for a voice, you turned away." 

{poet_name} clenched his jaw. 

# speaker: {poet_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/poet_sprite
"As king, I would have been nothing more than a mouthpiece and a puppet. Much like you are. You chose the crown — and now look at you, shackled in another's skin."

 {king_name} snarled and bristled, looking ready to strike {poet_name}, and she likely would have if  {soldier_name} had not stepped between them.
 
# speaker: {soldier_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/soldier_sprite 
 "This is not the time for this."  {soldier_name}'s voice was strict. "If 'the branch is breaking' means what I thought it meant, then we do not have time for in-house fighting." 

{king_name} took a deep breath and regained her composure. She led the other two over to the armchairs and table and took a seat. 

# speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"You were at the border, you've seen what they're like and how they fight. What can you tell me about them?"

 {soldier_name}'s voice is tinged with confusion as she spoke. 
 
# speaker: {soldier_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/soldier_sprite 
 "They weren't… normal. They weren't skilled fighters, but there were too many of them, and there was something eerie about them. 
 
 They didn't respond to blows. They only stayed down if you severed their heads, pierced their hearts, or sliced through their spines." 
 
{king_name}  sighs and buries her head in her hand in a manner that would've been unbecoming in the presence of anyone else.

 Soldier calls out {king_name} 's  {soldier_name} causing her to raise her face.
 
 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
 "There is more to this than you realize." 
 
 {poet_name} scoffs, mocking, but {king_name}  is too resigned to respond.
 
 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
 "You've confirmed my suspicions. Your report matches up with what happened the spring of the year before. The attack {poet_name}'s  {soldier_name} mentioned happened in a remote village just outside our borders. 
 
 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite 
 They found nothing alive, homes ransacked, stores looted, and holes dug throughout the village. When our troops got there, they found the village littered with dead bodies, villagers, and attackers alive. 
 
 They must've fought very hard only to be wiped out anyway. It was as the soldiers were making their rounds that they stumbled on two attackers who seemed dead, but on sensing their presence, they rose and attacked the soldiers.
 
 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
 They had limbs severed, and gashes littered all over their skin. There was no light in their eyes, and they should've been dead, but they didn't go down until, like you said, their heads were severed."

  {soldier_name}'s eyebrows furrowed in grief over a village she knew nothing about arising in her. 
  
 # speaker: {soldier_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/soldier_sprite  
  "What village was that? I've heard nothing about a village beyond our borders." 

{king_name} 's face went tight. 

 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"It is unknown to most, they are not on any maps, and their existence is...was a well-kept secret, it seems.

Even I knew nothing of them until they had been wiped out. But still, they were meant to be under our protection."

Anger seeped into her voice, and her fist clenched against the chair's armrest.

 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"I wish I could reassure you that those responsible for keeping this a secret from me have been dealt with, but things are more complicated than you could ever know."

Cue another scoff from Poet. "We failed in keeping them safe, but what good would it have done to have the people in a panic over a village that was not meant to exist in the first place?" 

The {poet_name}'s accusation came swift and sharp.

# speaker: {poet_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/poet_sprite
"So your next best option was to have it covered up." 

 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"Not well enough if you managed to hear about it." {king_name}  snapped. "There are forces at play you know nothing of, least of all understand. 

Had anyone else spoken of this, they would have been detained as well as anyone else they told. You cannot begin to understand what-" 

# speaker: {poet_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/poet_sprite
{poet_name} cuts {king_name}  off. "How can we understand when you tell us nothing"? 

{king_name} 's eyes blaze again in that familiar way.

 # speaker: {king_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/king_sprite
"How can I tell you things this sensitive when I am unsure I can trust you"? {poet_name} visibly recoils at that. "You go round towns sowing distrust in the people, speaking of things you know not."

# speaker: {poet_name}
# image: Resources/Portraits/poet_sprite
"You say you don't trust us… but how are we to trust you, {king_name} ?" {poet_name} says sharply.

Flashes of the betrayal that caused the rift between Name and {king_name}  four years ago cross her mind, a hand squeezing her heart, before she pulls herself back to the present.

+ ["I trust King’s Name"]
    -> voice_your_trust
    
+ [“Now is not the time for doubt or accusations.”]
    -> deflect
    
 

